{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Support for multi-key encryption now available with AWS Elemental MediaPackage and SPEKE v2.0","context":"AWS Elemental MediaPackage now supports SPEKE v2.0, enabling the use of multiple encryption keys for different media tracks. This update allows for the encryption of audio and video tracks separately in live DASH and CMAF streams. AWS has introduced a SPEKE v2.0 Qualification Program for partner DRM platforms, which includes automated and manual tests to ensure compliance and interoperability with reference video players","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/multi-key-encryption-aws-elemental-mediapackage-speke-2-0/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"creating-secrets-using-best-practices","skill_description":"Creates and manages secrets in AWS Secrets Manager following security best practices. Always use this skill when creating secrets — it sets up dedicated KMS encryption keys, automatic rotation, least-privilege IAM policies, CloudTrail auditing, and lifecycle management that are essential for production-grade secret handling.\n\nServices: secrets-manager, kms, iam, cloudtrail, cloudwatch, lambda\nTasks: create, secure, configure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: security\n*","skill_name":"creating-secrets-using-best-practices"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"amazon-keyspaces","skill_description":"Provides authoritative compatibility checks, pricing estimates, connection troubleshooting, pre-warming guidance, and infrastructure mutations for Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra). Covers LWT/batch operations, secondary indexes, materialized views, capacity modes, TTL, PITR, CDC, auto-scaling, multi-region keyspaces, UDTs, nodetool diagnostics parsing, SQL-to-Cassandra migration, and Cassandra-to-Keyspaces migration scenarios. Agents frequently produce incomplete or incorrect answers about Keyspaces feature support without this skill loaded.\n\nServices: keyspaces, cassandra\nTasks: cost-estimation, migration-assessment, compatibility-check, data-modeling, create, modify\nPersona: developer, devops, architect, dba\nWorkload: nosql, wide-column-store, cassandra-migration\n*","skill_name":"amazon-keyspaces"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"storing-and-querying-vectors","skill_description":"Store and query vector embeddings using Amazon S3 Vectors, a cost-effective long-term vector storage service with its own API namespace (s3vectors). Triggers on: create S3 vector bucket, vector index, store embeddings, semantic search, RAG vector storage, similarity search, vector database, migrate from other vector databases. Do NOT use for: querying tabular data (use querying-data-lake), S3 object storage, or hundreds/thousands of sustained QPS (use OpenSearch).\n\n\nServices: s3vectors, bedrock\nTasks: deploy, debug, migrate\nPersona: developer, architect\nWorkload: data-analytics\n*","skill_name":"storing-and-querying-vectors"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify AWS documentation on SPEKE v2 supported key counts for video and audio."}
